# Slack app credentials. Copy to .env, which is gitignored.
#
# Both come from one Slack app at https://api.slack.com/apps:
#   SLACK_APP_TOKEN  Basic Information -> App-Level Tokens, scope connections:write
#   SLACK_BOT_TOKEN  OAuth & Permissions, after installing the app to a workspace
SLACK_APP_TOKEN=xapp-...
SLACK_BOT_TOKEN=xoxb-...

# Where thread-to-agent bindings live. Defaults to ./state next to agents.toml.
# RICARDI_STATE_DIR=./state

# Claude Code credentials, for any deployment where nobody is logged in.
#
# The Agent SDK does not call an API: it spawns the `claude` CLI, which has to
# be signed in. Ricardi puts everything in this file into its environment, and
# the SDK hands its whole environment to the CLI it spawns, so one line here is
# the entire wiring.
#
# Set EXACTLY ONE of the two below, and never sign in on an always-on host: a
# stored login from `claude` or `/login` takes precedence over both of these,
# so it shadows whatever is here and then expires on its own schedule. See
# docs/running.md, "Credentials: pick one, and never sign in on the box".
# install-service.sh refuses if it finds both.
#
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY -- from the Anthropic Console. No scheduled expiry, and
# nothing an interactive login elsewhere can revoke, so this is the one for a
# box meant to run unattended. Bills per token to a Console account.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
#
# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN -- from `claude setup-token` (needs a browser once,
# on any machine). Stays on your Claude subscription. Its lifetime is not
# documented anywhere official and it does not refresh itself, so treat the
# expiry as unknown rather than annual. When it goes, Ricardi stops answering
# and Slack says nothing at all, which looks exactly like the host being down.
# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=
#
# Keep whichever you choose in this file and `chmod 600 .env`. Never in a
# launchd plist, a systemd unit or a service command line: all three are
# readable by anyone with an account on the machine.
